1. PREAMBLE & SOURCE-AVAILABLE STATUS
   The source code of the Liner software ("Software") is made publicly available
   to foster transparency, enable security review, and welcome collaborative
   community contributions to the official Liner upstream project.
   
   THIS SOFTWARE IS SOURCE-AVAILABLE. IT IS NOT PUBLIC DOMAIN NOR UNRESTRICTED
   OPEN SOURCE. ANY USE, COPYING, MODIFICATION, OR REDISTRIBUTION OUTSIDE THE
   EXPLICIT PERMISSIONS OF THIS LICENSE IS STRICTLY PROHIBITED.

   "Official Liner Services" means the servers, APIs and services operated or
   expressly designated by the copyright holders for the Software, including
   api.tryliner.fun, beta.tryliner.fun, staging.tryliner.fun and any successor
   or additional service they announce as official.

2. PERMITTED PERSONAL & EVALUATION USE
   Subject to the terms and limitations of this License, you are granted a
   personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, royalty-free license to:
   a) Inspect, study, and review the source code of the Software.
   b) Compile, build, and run the Software locally solely for your own personal,
      private, non-commercial, and non-monetized use.
   c) Modify the Software locally for testing, debugging, or personal experimentation,
      provided the modified Software keeps working only with the Official Liner
      Services as set out in Section 4(e).

3. UPSTREAM CONTRIBUTION PERMISSION
   You are expressly permitted to create forks, branches, and modifications of
   this Software for the SOLE PURPOSE of developing, preparing, and submitting
   contributions (including bug fixes, feature improvements, performance patches,
   and documentation) back to the official upstream repository:
   https://github.com/tryliner/desktop (or official Liner project repositories).

   By submitting any modification or Pull Request to the official upstream project,
   you grant the project maintainers a perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide,
   royalty-free, assignable right and license to use, incorporate, modify,
   relicense, and distribute your contribution as part of the Liner project.

